  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The transfer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RNA</mi></math> anticodon for messanger <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RNA</mi></math> codon&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math>, because in anticodon of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RNA</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> replaced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> replaced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> replaced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math></p><p>Here, C(cytosine) forms triple bond with G (guanine) and A (adenine) forms double bond with U (uracil).</p>",
